Let on_back_gesture claim a back gesture after keyboard input.

What: `Interactivity::on_back_gesture` hit-tests with `HitboxId::is_hovered_ignoring_last_input` instead of
`Hitbox::is_hovered`. Adds a window test with one row per input before the gesture (key press, touch).

Why: `Window::dispatch_event` leaves the input modality unchanged for `BackGesture` (window.rs, the
`last_input_modality` match), and `HitboxId::is_hovered` returns false while the modality is Keyboard. So after
any `KeyDown` no element can claim a back gesture until a mouse move or touch resets the modality. Keyboard
modality exists to hide hover under a stale cursor; a back gesture carries its own `start_position`, which
`dispatch_event` has just hit-tested, so the modality must not apply. Android's back key (parallax-android sends
it as a `BackGestureEvent`) arrives right after typing; iPad users with a hardware keyboard hit the same case.
Not platform-specific, so no cfg.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

